title: The Match-3 template
intro: Four gem-swapping levels with moves and goals, each opening once the one before is won. No code.
project: Match3 | Gem Rush

chapter: A menu of levels | Each one opens once the one before is won
scene: Main
say: The Match-3 template starts on a menu with a button for each level.
select: Level 2
explain: field:Button.NeedsSaved | Needs Saved | Level two's button opens once level one is saved as won.
expectvalue: Level 2.Button.NeedsSaved = complete-level1
deselect

chapter: A level | A board with moves and goals
scene: Level3
select: Board
explain: field:MatchBoard.Moves | Moves | Each level is a Match Board with its moves,
explain: field:MatchBoard.TargetScore | Target Score | a score to reach,
explain: field:MatchBoard.Collect | Collect | and gems to collect. Here, twenty emeralds, among stone blocks that never move.
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Collect = 3:20
select: Emeralds
explain: field:Counter.CountKind | Count Kind | The HUD down the left shows each goal with a counter.
select: Out of Moves
explain: field:Panel.OpenMessage | Open Message | A panel opens on Level Complete, and another on Out of Moves.
deselect

chapter: Play it | One swap
scene: Level1
select: Board
set: MatchBoard.Seed = 1
deselect
play
wait: 0.8
say: Click a gem, then the one beside it.
gameclick: 0.9, 3.5
wait: 0.3
gameclick: 0.9, 2.5
wait: 2
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Swaps = 1
expectvalue: Moves.Text.Value = Moves: 19
explain: game | Three in a row | Three gems lined up and cleared. Nineteen moves left to reach twelve hundred points.
stop
say: That's the Match-3 template. Duplicate a level and change its goals to make more.
